# Security response headers, served by Cloudflare Workers Static Assets (it honors _headers).
# Addresses the (unscored) Lighthouse security recommendations: a Content Security Policy,
# a strong HSTS policy (with preload), and clickjacking / MIME protections.
#
# CSP notes for maintainers:
#   - script-src is tight: 'self' + the inline anti-FOUC theme script ('unsafe-inline',
#     unavoidable on a static build with no per-request nonce) + the Cloudflare Web
#     Analytics beacon. It still blocks externally-loaded scripts.
#   - img-src / media-src allow https: so Sanity images (cdn.sanity.io) and editor-added
#     images / background videos load.
#   - frame-src lists the embeds actually used (YouTube, Vimeo, Google Maps). If a church
#     later adds a Subsplash / Planning Center script or iframe embed via the page builder,
#     add its origin to script-src / frame-src.
#   - connect-src covers the contact forms (Web3Forms) + analytics; add a newsletter or
#     Formspree origin here if one is enabled.
#   - frame-ancestors is 'self'. That is exactly right now that the Studio is EMBEDDED at
#     /studio (2026-08-28): the Presentation tool iframes /preview/* from the same origin.
#     Only re-add *.sanity.studio if you deliberately run a hosted Studio as well.
#   - Trusted Types is intentionally NOT enabled: require-trusted-types-for would break the
#     YouTube / Vimeo / Maps / analytics / embed scripts.
#
# THE EMBEDDED STUDIO'S OWN NEEDS (added 2026-08-28 with the /studio fold-in). A CSP tight
# enough for a static marketing site is NOT tight enough for a CMS shipped on the same
# origin, and every one of these was a real broken thing, not a precaution:
#   - connect-src  api.sanity.io + *.api.sanity.io   (queries, mutations, the listen API
#                                                     behind /preview/live)
#                  wss://*.api.sanity.io             (the Studio's realtime channel)
#                  *.apicdn.sanity.io                (CDN-backed reads)
#                  sanity-cdn.com + *.sanity-cdn.com (the Studio's module/version ping;
#                                                     blocked, it logs "Failed to fetch
#                                                     version for package")
#   - font-src     design-system-static.sanity.io    (the Studio's own Inter)
#                  fonts.gstatic.com                 (StudioLayout injects the brand faces)
#   - style-src    fonts.googleapis.com              (same brand-font stylesheet)
#   - worker-src   'self' blob:                      (the Studio uses blob workers)
#   - img-src      already https: data:, which covers cdn.sanity.io and blob previews;
#                  blob: is added for the image editor's local crops.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self' https://design-system-static.sanity.io https://fonts.gstatic.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' blob: https://api.web3forms.com https://cloudflareinsights.com https://api.sanity.io https://*.api.sanity.io wss://*.api.sanity.io https://*.apicdn.sanity.io https://cdn.sanity.io https://sanity-cdn.com https://*.sanity-cdn.com https://api.unsplash.com; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://www.google.com https://maps.google.com; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; upgrade-insecure-requests
